course: dictionary
lesson: 7274
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the clues around them to know which one is meant. «The male Hercules beetle has two long horns, used like pincers to lift and throw rivals.» The words «used like» tell you that the horns are not really pincers. They work like pincers, gripping and lifting.
explain: Pincers can mean a crab's claws, a tool, or even a battle plan. Look at what the sentence is about. If it talks about crabs, lobsters or scorpions, pincers are claws. If it talks about pulling nails, pincers are a tool with two handles and curved jaws.
explain: A pincer movement is a battle plan. Two groups attack an enemy from both sides, so the enemy is trapped in the middle. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A pincer is one claw of a crab, lobster or scorpion, and it is used for gripping.
fact: Pincers, usually said in the plural, is a tool with two handles and two curved jaws for gripping things or pulling out nails.
fact: A pincer movement is an attack in which two groups come at an enemy from both sides.
fact: In science, minibeasts such as earwigs and scorpions have pincers.
fact: «Used like pincers» means something works in the same way as pincers, even if it is not a real pair of pincers.
exercise: «The crab snapped its pincers at the fish.» What are the pincers in this sentence? | *The claws of a crab | A tool with two handles for pulling nails | Two groups attacking from both sides | A kind of fish
exercise: Dad used pincers to pull the bent nail out of the wood. What are pincers here? | A cooking pot | *A tool with two handles and curved jaws for gripping | A pair of crab claws
exercise: The generals planned a pincer movement, with two armies attacking the enemy from both sides. What is a pincer movement? | A dance done by soldiers | A slow walk through the forest | *An attack where two groups come at an enemy from both sides | A sort of crab race
test: «The scorpion lifted its pincers to guard itself.» What are the pincers? | *The claws of a scorpion | A tool for pulling nails | A pair of curved scissors | Two armies on a hill
test: The history book said the soldiers trapped the enemy in a pincer movement. What does this mean? | The enemy was given a gift | The soldiers were lost in the mist | *The enemy was attacked from both sides | The soldiers went home early
exam: «The male Hercules beetle has two long horns, used like pincers to lift and throw rivals.» What does «used like pincers» mean? | *The horns work in the same way as pincers, gripping and lifting | The horns are two armies attacking from both sides | The horns are real crab claws | The horns are a tool for pulling nails
